/*
We are given, for one relay station:
- current ranking of N teams
- for each team, the displayed change from the previous station

If a team is currently at rank i (1-indexed) and its displayed change is d,
then its previous rank was i + d
because:
  positive d => moved up by d places
  negative d => moved down by -d places

Thus the previous ranking is uniquely determined if all previous ranks
are within [1, N] and all are distinct. Otherwise, impossible.

Answer:
- 1 if the reconstructed previous order is valid
- 0 otherwise
(mod 1,000,000,007, though only 0 or 1 can occur)

Input format assumed:
N
team1 d1
team2 d2
...
teamN dN

where the lines are given in current rank order from 1st to Nth.

The team names are irrelevant for counting; only the rank changes matter.
To be robust, we read each line as:
- a string token (team name / identifier)
- an integer d

If the actual judge uses identifiers as integers, this still works.
*/

public class Main {
    static final long MOD = 1_000_000_007L;

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);

        Integer nObj = fs.nextIntNullable();
        if (nObj == null) return;
        int N = nObj;

        boolean[] used = new boolean[N + 1];
        boolean ok = true;

        for (int currentRank = 1; currentRank <= N; currentRank++) {
            fs.next(); // team name / identifier, not needed
            int diff = fs.nextInt();

            int prevRank = currentRank + diff;
            if (prevRank < 1 || prevRank > N || used[prevRank]) {
                ok = false;
            } else {
                used[prevRank] = true;
            }
        }

        System.out.println(ok ? 1 % MOD : 0);
    }

    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        String next() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
            } while (c != -1 && c <= ' ');
            if (c == -1) return null;

            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            while (c != -1 && c > ' ') {
                sb.append((char) c);
                c = read();
            }
            return sb.toString();
        }

        Integer nextIntNullable() throws IOException {
            String s = next();
            if (s == null) return null;
            return Integer.parseInt(s);
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return Integer.parseInt(next());
        }
    }
}

